// check: refuse E_InitPerformsOwnOp
// The state init's sibling carrier: a handler's config DEFAULT performing an
// op that handler itself answers. Defaults and inits lower into one `inits`
// list, so one class covers both — measured, not assumed, and this fixture
// is what holds that true as the lowering changes.
//
// The state-init half was armed at pin 362ac8b1eeae; this half was the
// unmeasured sibling that landing named, and it was already covered on the
// first probe. What was NOT true was the message, which said "state init"
// for both carriers until this fixture made the imprecision visible.
effect F { g() -> Int }
handler hf(k: Int = g()) with s = 1 {
  g() => resume(k),
}
fn main(q) = (g()) ~> hf
